WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:14,260
I recently had a PET scan that showed an additional nodule on the left lobe of my thyroid

00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:20,580
where previously I had the right only.

00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:24,500
The doctor wanted to remove half my thyroid, well, it was on the right and I declined,

00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:30,900
and certainly he will now concertoal want to remove the whole thyroid.

00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:33,420
What could I do to shrink these nodules?

00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:42,020
Well, again, you want to diagnose what they're from and if they're cancerous,

00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:49,060
or if they are from hypothyroidism or Hashimoto's.

00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:51,060
So what will cause thyroid nodules?

00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:55,620
Well, decrease in iodine will cause thyroid nodules.

00:00:55,620 --> 00:00:57,900
It's your iodine levels testing.

00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:03,180
Hashimoto's, the number one cause of thyroid nodules, Hashimoto's.

00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:07,460
If you had a biopsy, the other nodule biopsy that was cancerous,

00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:10,980
that does not mean the other this new nodule is cancer.

00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:16,940
So if you're going to get this biopsy, that will tell you the answer to that.

00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:22,340
But to remember, the number one cause of thyroid nodules is Hashimoto's.

00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:27,740
So don't think that you can't have more than one big going on.

00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:31,780
So how do you diagnose Hashimoto's?

00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:36,700
You have to do a full thyroid blood flow file.

00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:45,260
So full thyroid test is going to include your T3, your T4.

00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:49,380
And that's going to be three T3, three T4.

00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:51,620
It's going to include your TSH.

00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:59,820
It's going to include your TPO antibodies and your thyroid globular antibodies.

00:01:59,860 --> 00:02:06,420
And it's going to include reverse T3 would be good to have it out there.

00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:16,220
And so just make sure that you look at the biggest picture that you possibly can on your thyroid.

00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:22,100
These tests your thyroid antibodies, sorry, these two tests your TPO antibodies

00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:27,380
and your thyroid globular antibodies are going to diagnose Hashimoto's.

00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:31,980
So if you have TPO and or thyroid globular antibodies that are elevated,

00:02:31,980 --> 00:02:34,300
you have Hashimoto's.

00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:38,420
If your thyroid is hyperactive and you have either one of these,

00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:40,700
then you have what's called Graves' disease.

00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:45,380
And that's a much more serious thing that you have to take care of in a different way.

00:02:45,380 --> 00:02:48,620
But Hashimoto's is the number one cause of increased nodules.

00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:52,820
And don't think even if you have thyroid cancer that will diagnose,

00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:54,580
that you can't also have Hashimoto's.

